  "name": "stainless",
  "description": "Stainless is a lightweight, flexible testing framework for Rust implemented as a compiler syntax extension. It provides a domain-specific language for defining hierarchical test suites with scoped setup and teardown hooks. By performing direct AST manipulation, it expands high-level block structures into idiomatic Rust test modules and benchmark functions.",
